{%- comment -%}
  Ambient wallpaper — a moving background that costs no bandwidth.

  WHY IT IS BUILT THIS WAY. An animation is free only when it runs on the compositor,
  which means it may change `transform` and `opacity` and nothing else. Those get handed
  to the GPU as a cached layer. Animate `background-position`, a gradient's colour stops,
  `box-shadow` or any geometry property instead and the browser repaints every frame on
  the main thread — on a mid-range Android that is the difference between roughly no CPU
  and a third of it, which shows up as jank while scrolling and a warm phone. Most of the
  "animated gradient background" snippets on the internet animate `background-position`.
  Those are the ones that hurt.

  So: three big radial gradients, painted once, moved with `translate3d` and `scale`.

  NO BLUR BY DEFAULT. A blurred solid circle looks similar but has to rasterise a very
  large blurred layer and hold it in GPU memory. A radial gradient that fades to
  transparent gives the same soft edge for nothing, so blur is an optional extra rather
  than the mechanism.

  IT CANNOT SLOW THE PAGE DOWN. No requests, no images, no JavaScript; the CSS rides
  along in a stylesheet the page already loads. Being decorative and empty it can never
  become the LCP element, and with no script there is nothing to pause when the tab is
  hidden — the browser simply stops compositing it.

  OFF BY DEFAULT. It is decoration, and the store's problem is that 99% of visitors leave
  without adding anything to the cart. Shipping it alongside a conversion change would
  also make that change unattributable. Turn it on deliberately, on its own.

  ON THE AUDIENCE. This store sells to people with OCD, intrusive thoughts and
  hypervigilance, reading long careful copy that tells them to read each page once. A
  restless background works against that, and for some people motion is a genuine
  sensory trigger. Hence very slow defaults, low opacity, and an honest
  `prefers-reduced-motion` branch that stops it dead rather than merely slowing it.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if section.settings.enabled -%}
  <div class="amb" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="amb__blob amb__blob--a"></span>
    <span class="amb__blob amb__blob--b"></span>
    {%- if section.settings.color_c != blank -%}
      <span class="amb__blob amb__blob--c"></span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- style -%}
    .amb {
      position: fixed;
      inset: 0;
      z-index: -1;
      overflow: hidden;
      pointer-events: none;
      /* Clips the blobs and isolates their painting from the rest of the document. */
      contain: layout paint style;
    }

    .amb__blob {
      position: absolute;
      display: block;
      border-radius: 50%;
      opacity: {{ section.settings.opacity | divided_by: 100.0 }};
      {%- if section.settings.blur > 0 %}
        filter: blur({{ section.settings.blur }}px);
      {%- endif %}
      /* Promotes each blob to its own layer so the drift never repaints the page. */
      will-change: transform;
    }

    .amb__blob--a {
      top: -18%;
      left: -12%;
      width: 62vmax;
      height: 62vmax;
      background: radial-gradient(circle at 50% 50%, {{ section.settings.color_a }} 0%, transparent 68%);
      animation: amb-drift-a {{ section.settings.speed }}s ease-in-out infinite alternate;
    }

    .amb__blob--b {
      bottom: -22%;
      right: -14%;
      width: 56vmax;
      height: 56vmax;
      background: radial-gradient(circle at 50% 50%, {{ section.settings.color_b }} 0%, transparent 68%);
      animation: amb-drift-b {{ section.settings.speed | times: 1.4 | round }}s ease-in-out infinite alternate;
    }

    {%- if section.settings.color_c != blank %}
      .amb__blob--c {
        top: 28%;
        left: 38%;
        width: 44vmax;
        height: 44vmax;
        background: radial-gradient(circle at 50% 50%, {{ section.settings.color_c }} 0%, transparent 68%);
        animation: amb-drift-c {{ section.settings.speed | times: 0.8 | round }}s ease-in-out infinite alternate;
      }
    {%- endif %}

    @keyframes amb-drift-a {
      from { transform: translate3d(-8%, -5%, 0) scale(1); }
      to   { transform: translate3d(10%, 7%, 0) scale(1.18); }
    }

    @keyframes amb-drift-b {
      from { transform: translate3d(7%, 6%, 0) scale(1.12); }
      to   { transform: translate3d(-9%, -8%, 0) scale(1); }
    }

    @keyframes amb-drift-c {
      from { transform: translate3d(-6%, 8%, 0) scale(1); }
      to   { transform: translate3d(8%, -6%, 0) scale(1.25); }
    }

    {%- unless section.settings.show_on_mobile %}
      @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
        .amb { display: none; }
      }
    {%- endunless %}

    /*
      Smaller blobs on a phone: vmax on a tall screen means the width, so a 62vmax circle
      is roughly two viewport-heights across. Cheaper to composite and it reads the same.
    */
    @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
      .amb__blob--a, .amb__blob--b, .amb__blob--c { width: 78vw; height: 78vw; }
    }

    /* Stopped, not slowed. Anyone asking for less motion means none. */
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .amb__blob {
        animation: none;
        transform: none;
        will-change: auto;
      }
    }
  {%- endstyle -%}

  {%- if section.settings.transparent_sections -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Sections paint their own background colour, and every one of them defaults to the
      same colour as the page, so by default they sit on top of the wallpaper and hide
      it completely. This clears them. It is a blunt instrument on purpose — the precise
      alternative is to set the background of individual sections to none in the theme
      editor, which is the better move once you know which sections you want it behind.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- style -%}
      .shopify-section,
      .page-wrapper,
      main.content-for-layout {
        background-color: transparent !important;
      }
    {%- endstyle -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Ambient wallpaper",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "A slow moving glow behind the whole site. Pure CSS — no images, no video, no scripts, and nothing extra to download."
    },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "enabled", "label": "Enabled", "default": false },
    { "type": "color", "id": "color_a", "label": "First colour", "default": "#39FF14" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "color_b", "label": "Second colour", "default": "#BF00FF" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "color_c", "label": "Third colour", "info": "Optional. Leave empty for two." },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "opacity",
      "label": "Strength",
      "min": 4,
      "max": 60,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 22,
      "info": "Keep it low. It is atmosphere behind text, not a feature."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "speed",
      "label": "Cycle length",
      "min": 20,
      "max": 90,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "s",
      "default": 55,
      "info": "Longer is calmer. Under about 30s starts to read as movement rather than atmosphere."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "blur",
      "label": "Extra blur",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 120,
      "step": 10,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "info": "The gradients are already soft. Blur costs GPU memory, so leave it at 0 unless you want a specific look."
    },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_on_mobile", "label": "Show on mobile", "default": true },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "transparent_sections",
      "label": "Let it show through sections",
      "default": false,
      "info": "Sections paint their own background and will hide the wallpaper. Turn this on to clear them all at once. If a section is meant to be a different colour, set that one's background explicitly instead."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Ambient wallpaper" }]
}
{% endschema %}
